the list system means that in  many ways  it might appear to benefit the  independence movement on paper but what  you're doing is making this election  all about cat fighting in the  independence movement  nicola sturgeon versus alex salmond i  think some people might say well hang on  how can you say that you're trying to  help the s p  by quitting no this is about delivering  that independent super majority  i'll be 63 next month sophie throughout  my life  scotland has rejected the tories not  just boris johnson but thatcher heath  and others before  and continually were left with the tory  government we now stand with our economy  threatened by brexit  with our health service threatened by  trade deals upcoming nuclear weapons  escalating that are based on the clyde  that's simply unacceptable the time has  come for scotland to decide its own  destiny  you think the snp alone can't defeat  boris johnson and cannot  deliver independence that's that's  arithmetic's clear in 2016 the snp did  not get a majority  they had one million list votes and  returned four msps  the independent super majority could be  delivered by the alba party  on list the yes movement the  independence movement is a broad church  it encompasses  more than one political party and it  encompasses many people  in other or no political parties so we  believe that the time has come for that  independence movement to come together  reflected by more than one political  party but to make sure that there's a  scottish people who prevail and it's the  scottish people who decide  and that will be the scottish parliament  that will then confront boris johnson  after the 6th of may so this is all  about helping the snp  i'm a bit baffled by their reaction to  it all to be honest um after you  defected in blackford said  of you he's been an increasing  embarrassment to many in the snp  and his departure is somewhat of a  relief doesn't sound like you're leaving  the best of terms  well snp speak for themselves i've made  it clear that i'll be supporting a  former colleague in east lothian it's be  up to individuals in alberta to decide  what they do  uh but the yes movement the independence  movement is a broad church  it's not simply the snp the snp  on their own it failed to achieve a  majority in 2016.  alba party can ensure that there is an  independence  majority in 2021 we won't be beholden to  the snp because we are  not the snp but we certainly start  campaign for independence and we  certainly stand on the radical tradition  of the radical policies  that the snp used to and i believe in  many instances still support  used to stand on it's a bit of a slip of  the tongue there  no well there are issues that i think  have caused many people concerning the  snp  that's why some have come over just  today we had the uh  equalities officer from the snp coming  over  along with a colleague the other party  now has more mps  in scotland than the labour party we are  here to stay  we are going to deliver a result in 2021  in the mention  to make sure that it's in the super  majority that is delivered  this election is already becoming about  independence  we've got to make sure that the outcome  is about an independent majority within  the scottish parliament  and that allows scotland's democracy to  choose we cannot go on under boris  johnson  we've had austerity inflicted it's going  to increase  the time has come for scotland to go its  own way and to do so  would require to be an independent  nation i'm just trying to work out why  you think  alex salmond is the man to help deliver  the independence that you want because  according to the latest opinion poll for  sky news  nicholas sturgeon's got a plus 21  approval rating among scots  plus 2067 among independent supporters  alex salmond's approval rating is minus  60  and even 68 of yes supporters have an  unfavorable view of him i mean do you  really think he's an  asset to the independence course well i  think alex almond was pivotal to the  independence cause and delivered the  2014  referendum but this is not it and he  wasn't  and that's why others have come on board  just yesterday we had corey wilson a  former  snp mp joined the party just today we  have councillor lynn anderson  the equalities officer for the snp they  put their trust and faith in mr salmond  and exactly the same as a scottish jury  acquitted him on all charges  a jury that was overwhelmingly  represented by women  uh you say very rightly of course that  he was  acquitted by that jury nicholas scotland  nicholas sturgeon says though in a  scotland on sunday interview today that  serious questions have been raised  about the appropriateness of his  behavior towards women while he held the  highest office in the land  i think that raises real questions about  the appropriateness of any return to  public office  do you think that alex salmon still has  serious questions to answer as nicholas  sturgeon says  no we've had two court cases he has been  successful in both a civil and indeed a  criminal court action  that is behind us we go forward and  indeed it's from this  sturgeon to our school but why others in  the snp who behaved inappropriately were  not dealt with  but we're going to keep this positive on  independence we're not here to battle  with the snp we are here to win  on the list and that will be contesting  against the snp because they can't  deliver  that independence super majority but we  are part of the wider independence  movement it is not the prerogative  of one political party there is more  than one political party pursuing  independence in scotland  and i will continue to campaign for  independence target my fire against the  unionist parties who are once again  seeking to coalesce  and i would hope that other political  parties would recognize that it's a  common cause of independence  not name throwing that they should be  carrying out now of course  as you say you know alexander's always  denied all of the harassment allegations  made against him  he was cleared of all the charges in  court important state  but in the court case his defense lawyer  did say i'm not here to suggest he  always behaved well or he couldn't have  been a better man on occasions  because he certainly could have been  better and alex almond has previously  said you know i'm no saint  i've got flaws are you comfortable  being in a party with him as leader well  let him without sin cast the first stone  since we're  speaking on a sunday equally you're just  asking a tory minister about behavior  within the tories  i think the people i'm most concerned  about it would be allowing boris johnson  to continue  running the roost in scotland along with  the likes of pretty patel or matt  hancock  so when it comes to this i think the snp  the alba party  and indeed the politicians in scotland  most parties stand far above that  so i'm comfortable and as i say that was  shown by corey wilson  and indeed lynn anderson today showing  that they have every faith in him  but this is about the alba party  delivering  that independence super majority it's  not about any individual  and it's not about name throwing or  tittle title and i hope that people in  my former party will reflect  upon who's actually shown commitment in  the past  and who's still showing commitment in  the future and that we should show some  common cause  rather than as i say seek to divide the  independence movement  just finally at the last election you of  course stood under the snp  banner you're now representing a  different party  shouldn't you hold a by-election  no i'll be doing what has been done  before at the outset of the scottish  parliament donald jr and labour mps  exercised the dual mandate  during the parliament that i served in  alex hammond and indeed john swinney the  deputy first minister of the scottish  parliament  uh stood on a dual mandate and  represented both westminster and  holyrood  so i'll be seeking to represent  hollywood as well as retaining and  continue to serve my constituents in  east london  okay thank you very much for being on  the program kenny mccaskill there  thank you

